# Wait for an explicit ask

Do not create Jira issues, git branches, commits, pushes, or pull requests unless the user explicitly asks for that action in this conversation.

Implementing or finishing code is not permission to:

- create or clone a Jira story, task, bug, or sub-task
- transition a Jira issue, assign it, or comment on it
- create, rename, or switch git branches
- `git commit`, `git push`, or open a PR

If a project guide describes a one-branch / one-PR / one-story workflow, follow it only after the user asks. Until then, edit files in the current workspace and leave git and Jira alone.

Do not use Jira or Atlassian skills (create-task, capture-tasks-from-meeting-notes, spec-to-backlog, triage-issue) unless the user asked to create or change tickets.
